[Keep Skating When Out of Juice]
author=Aggressive Inline PC port
description=An empty juice meter no longer ends a Career run. (tested in PCSX2)
patch=1,EE,00246248,word,00000000 // Death by Juice = 0 (game: 1)

[Juice Drain 50%]
author=Aggressive Inline PC port
description=The juice meter empties half as fast. (tested in PCSX2)
patch=1,EE,00247BF8,word,3F800000 // Max Juice Degradation/sec = 1 (game: 2)

[No Juice Drain]
author=Aggressive Inline PC port
description=The juice meter only goes down when you crash. (tested in PCSX2)
patch=1,EE,00247BF8,word,00000000 // Max Juice Degradation/sec = 0 (game: 2)

[Juice Lost on Crash 50%]
author=Aggressive Inline PC port
description=A crash takes half as much juice. (partly tested: value checked in PCSX2 memory, crash not played)
patch=1,EE,00247BC8,word,3E800000 // Juice Lost/Level on crash = 0.25 (game: 0.5)

[Cheat: Low Gravity Wall Ride]
author=Aggressive Inline PC port
description=Wall rides last longer. The game's own cheat, always on, without its code (and without setting the cheat bits the codes leave in the career data). (partly tested: value checked in PCSX2 memory, effect not played)
patch=1,EE,0024A3E8,word,40400000 // Wall Ride Gravity = 3 (game: 12); as the game's cheat code sets it (0x001AA628)

[Cheat: Juice Regeneration]
author=Aggressive Inline PC port
description=The juice meter fills up by itself. The game's own cheat, always on, without its code (and without setting the cheat bits the codes leave in the career data). (tested in PCSX2)
patch=1,EE,00247BF8,word,BE4CCCCD // Max Juice Degradation/sec = -0.2 (game: 2); as the game's cheat code sets it (0x001AA628)

[Cheat: Invulnerability]
author=Aggressive Inline PC port
description=Crashes cost no juice. The game's own cheat, always on, without its code (and without setting the cheat bits the codes leave in the career data). (partly tested: value checked in PCSX2 memory, effect not played)
patch=1,EE,00247BC8,word,00000000 // Juice Lost/Level on crash = 0 (game: 0.5); as the game's cheat code sets it (0x001AA628)

[Cheat: Perfect Grind]
author=Aggressive Inline PC port
description=Grinds never lose balance. The game's own cheat, always on, without its code (and without setting the cheat bits the codes leave in the career data). (partly tested: values checked in PCSX2 memory, effect not played)
patch=1,EE,00249C68,word,00000000 // Grind Balance Factor = 0 (game: 0.0001); as the game's cheat code sets it (0x001AA628)
patch=1,EE,00249CC8,word,00000000 // Grind Balance Init = 0 (game: 0.004); as the game's cheat code sets it (0x001AA628)

[Cheat: Perfect Handplant]
author=Aggressive Inline PC port
description=Hand plants (stalls) never lose balance. The game's own cheat, always on, without its code (and without setting the cheat bits the codes leave in the career data). (partly tested: values checked in PCSX2 memory, effect not played)
patch=1,EE,00249E78,word,00000000 // Stall Balance Factor = 0 (game: 0.00012); as the game's cheat code sets it (0x001AA628)
patch=1,EE,00249ED8,word,00000000 // Stall Balance Init = 0 (game: 0.003); as the game's cheat code sets it (0x001AA628)

[Cheat: Perfect Manual]
author=Aggressive Inline PC port
description=Manuals never lose balance. The game's own cheat, always on, without its code (and without setting the cheat bits the codes leave in the career data). (partly tested: values checked in PCSX2 memory, effect not played)
